course: dictionary
lesson: 6318
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look the same but mean different things. «MOT» is one of them. «In the UK, cars older than three years need a yearly test called the MOT.» Here the MOT is a safety check that a car must pass before it can be driven on the road.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is right. The sentence talks about cars, roads and safety, so the MOT must be the car test. Check by swapping in your meaning: «a car that fails must be repaired» only makes sense with the test meaning.
explain: The other meaning is rare and comes from French. A «bon mot» is a clever, witty remark, a short saying that makes people smile. You will mostly find it in grown-up books, so look at the words around it to see which meaning the writer means.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, and context shows which one is used.
fact: An MOT is a yearly test that cars more than a few years old must pass to show they are safe to drive on the road.
fact: A «bon mot» is a clever, witty remark, and «mot» is the French word it comes from.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «In the UK, cars over three years old need a yearly safety test called an MOT.» What is an MOT? | *A yearly test to check a car is safe to drive | A type of car engine | A clever, witty remark | A place to park
exercise: Mum says, «The car failed its MOT, so the garage has to fix it.» What does failed suggest? | It won a prize | It was taken for a long drive | It was painted red | *It did not pass the safety test
exercise: «The writer's bon mot made everyone laugh.» What does bon mot mean? | A rude word | *A clever, witty remark | A quiet whisper | A yearly car test
test: «Parents take the car for its MOT every year.» What is the MOT for? | To make the car faster | *To check the car is safe to drive | To find lost keys | To clean the car inside
test: «Her bon mot at dinner had everyone smiling.» What is a bon mot? | *A clever, witty saying | A long, boring speech | A kind of car | A type of cake
exam: «A car that fails its MOT must be repaired before it can be driven legally.» What must happen to a car that fails its MOT? | It must go to a new town | *It must be repaired before it is driven | It must be painted red | It must be sold
